Then, we calculate the logarithm of `n` to base 3 using the `Math.log()` and `Math.log(3)` methods.

Finally, we check if the result is an integer by taking the remainder of `(int) log3n % 1`, which will be 0 if `log3n` is an integer.

This solution has a time complexity of O(1) and does not use loops or recursion.

